This is not true.  "Psychological addiction" and physical addiction are
very different.  Some people have "addictive personalities" which could
lead them to lose control over whether they play video games or whatnot,
but this is a personality disorder that has nothing to do with physical
addiction.  If these people weren't "addicted" to video games, they would
be "addicted" to something else.  Words like "obsessive" and "compulsive"
are better for this.

Video games can be very good at developing fine-grained hand-eye
coordination, quick reaction time, and thinking under pressure.  They
can also be a waste of time and money.

Professional drug warriors and associated hysterics use the term
"pyschological addiction" to destroy any distinction between addictive and
non-addictive illegal drugs.  Anything at all can be "psychologically 
addictive".  This is a case where hyperbole has become so routine that 
it has a drastic effect on people's thinking.  This "psychological
addiction" meme should be stamped out.

